# =============================================================================
# mobile-app env template (this file is tracked; copy to .env.local to use)
# =============================================================================
# Expo loads `.env.local` (gitignored) automatically. Any var prefixed with
# EXPO_PUBLIC_ is inlined into the client bundle at build time.
#
# Copy this file → .env.local and uncomment / edit the line you need.
#
# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# EXPO_PUBLIC_API_BASE_URL
# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Flips the app between mock-first dev (MSW intercepts everything) and the
# real backend (MSW skipped, network goes straight to this URL).
#
#   Empty / unset  → MSW intercepts every request. Demo creds come from
#                    packages/mock-data (alice/alice1234, bob/bob12345,
#                    demo/demo1234) and the contract matches
#                    @multimodal/api-contract exactly.
#
#   Non-empty      → MSW is skipped in App.tsx and api.ts / auth.ts hit this
#                    URL directly. MUST include any path prefix the backend
#                    expects (FastAPI skeleton mounts everything under /api/v1)
#                    so call sites in api.ts / auth.ts can stay path-only
#                    (e.g. `/auth/login`, `/me`).
#
# Examples:
#
#   Local SSH tunnel (Mac → paper3-server, port 9000):
#     http://127.0.0.1:9000/api/v1
#
#   Remote (sandbox / staging):
#     https://api.example.com/api/v1
#
# To run the SSH tunnel from a Mac dev machine:
#
#     nohup ~/.ssh/bin/paper3-ssh \
#         -N -L 9000:127.0.0.1:9000 \
#         -o ServerAliveInterval=60 \
#         -o ExitOnForwardFailure=yes \
#         > /tmp/paper3-tunnel.log 2>&1 &
#
# Verify the tunnel before starting Expo:
#
#     curl -s http://127.0.0.1:9000/health
# =============================================================================

# EXPO_PUBLIC_API_BASE_URL=